1031
00:57:18.440 --> 00:57:22.240
We're all fighting against atrophy here,
and these digital items are beholden to

1032
00:57:22.280 --> 00:57:23.560
their physical components.

1033
00:57:23.560 --> 00:57:26.240
That's just kind of how it is.

1034
00:57:26.240 --> 00:57:29.400
So when it comes to storage solution,
the most important thing

1035
00:57:29.400 --> 00:57:31.520
is to back up your data
in more than one place.

1036
00:57:31.520 --> 00:57:34.640
I cannot stress that enough,
whether it's online or locally

1037
00:57:34.640 --> 00:57:37.640
or on an external drive, doesn't matter.

1038
00:57:37.680 --> 00:57:40.560
Back up your data
in more than one place. Two is good.

1039
00:57:40.560 --> 00:57:41.880
Even more is even better though.

1040
00:57:41.880 --> 00:57:44.240
Like back it up as many places as you can.

1041
00:57:44.240 --> 00:57:45.840
For many people,
that's probably going to mean

1042
00:57:45.840 --> 00:57:48.120
like mirroring external drives, right?

1043
00:57:48.120 --> 00:57:50.600
That's kind of the one of the ways
to go about doing it.

1044
00:57:50.600 --> 00:57:51.640
I think a lot of people do.

1045
00:57:51.640 --> 00:57:54.160
So if that's your route,
what I want to recommend

1046
00:57:54.160 --> 00:57:58.000
is that you definitely go with hard disk
drives over solid state drives.

1047
00:57:58.360 --> 00:58:01.920
SSDs are faster and better for daily work
because of that,

1048
00:58:01.920 --> 00:58:05.280
but HDDs are superior for long
term storage

1049
00:58:05.280 --> 00:58:09.160
if you use them correctly, because,
I mean, they're hard disk drives, right?

1050
00:58:09.160 --> 00:58:11.440
They've got a magnetic platter in there.

1051
00:58:11.440 --> 00:58:15.040
So they use that platter to store the data
rather than electrical

1052
00:58:15.640 --> 00:58:16.680
electrical charges.

1053
00:58:16.680 --> 00:58:18.960
Excuse me to store that data.

1054
00:58:18.960 --> 00:58:22.120
SSDs need to be periodically charged
to avoid data loss.

1055
00:58:22.120 --> 00:58:25.120
So I highly recommend just grabbing an HD.

1056
00:58:25.280 --> 00:58:28.360
Put in all your files on there
and then setting it away.

1057
00:58:28.400 --> 00:58:28.840
You know, like

1058
00:58:28.840 --> 00:58:32.640
don't don't chuck it obviously, but don't,
you know, don't access it regularly.

1059
00:58:32.640 --> 00:58:33.640
Don't overwrite that data.

1060
00:58:33.640 --> 00:58:35.400
Just put it in cold storage.

1061
00:58:35.400 --> 00:58:36.920
Just leave it be.

1062
00:58:36.920 --> 00:58:40.520
SSDs are fantastic for their speed
and they're very stable, but HDD

1063
00:58:40.560 --> 00:58:42.000
better for long term.

1064
00:58:42.000 --> 00:58:45.520
There are also long term
archival cloud storage services like,

1065
00:58:45.640 --> 00:58:48.520
I don't know,
Amazon, Glacier or Backblaze or

1066
00:58:48.520 --> 00:58:51.520
things like that
that are not like typical web hosting.

1067
00:58:51.760 --> 00:58:52.360
They're cloud

1068
00:58:52.360 --> 00:58:55.120
based services which are specifically
designed for long term storage.

1069
00:58:55.120 --> 00:58:57.840
You put your files in and you don't
access them for a long, long time.

1070
00:58:57.840 --> 00:59:01.120
And when you do want to access them,
you have to request access.

1071
00:59:01.480 --> 00:59:03.960
And then you get a little bit of a charge
for like the download.

1072
00:59:03.960 --> 00:59:07.360
But those are also fantastic services.

1073
00:59:07.440 --> 00:59:10.600
We use a more web
like a standard web service for the next,

1074
00:59:10.600 --> 00:59:14.560
because we want people to actually be able
to view those works through a browser.

1075
00:59:14.560 --> 00:59:17.120
So that can also be appealing to people.

1076
00:59:17.120 --> 00:59:18.400
But whatever you route, you go.

1077
00:59:18.400 --> 00:59:22.080
I really, really just want to emphasize
back it up in multiple places.

1078
00:59:22.160 --> 00:59:24.120
Always do that no matter what.

1079
00:59:24.120 --> 00:59:26.480
Multiple places one, two, three, four.

1080
00:59:26.480 --> 00:59:27.840
As many as you can get.

